      "message": "Yes, with the current implementation of charge_get_state(), we have all the current returns from it handled in led_get_state() so we shouldn\u0027t hit the case of getting STATE_DEFAULT back.  \n\nHowever, we have an issue we\u0027re fixing in another platform where if we reference an led_state which hasn\u0027t been defined in the led_bat_state_table, then line 98 can hit a divide by zero error and crash the EC.  I\u0027d like to avoid the possibility for any similar crashes in the event that, for example, a new power state is added for another project without altering led_get_state() here.  It\u0027s up to you how defensively you\u0027d like to program it though.",
